The idea is exactly the same as on pages 172--173 of \cite{Palmer2018Twistedhomologicalstability}, so we just give a sketch of how to adapt it. By Proposition \ref{p:decomposition}, Lemma \ref{l:degree-height} and Shapiro's lemma for covering spaces (see Lemma 6.1 of \cite{Palmer2018Twistedhomologicalstability}) there are natural isomorphisms
